---
title: Saving additional attributes when adding Attachments
keywords: 'ibm maximo, maximo mobile, attachments, customization'
date: 12 November 2025
hiddenFromSearch: false
---

## About this task

You can include custom controls when adding attachments and link them to attachment attributes.

## Prerequisites

This feature is only supported with the `touch` theme. The attribute `allow-naming` must be set to true when declaring the attachment list in the application xml. The attributes with which you link custom controls can be persistent or non-persistent. They must be valid DOCLINK attributes and must be included in the object structure of the attachment datasource.

## Procedure

The custom controls are added using the `custom-options` slot on attachment lists. The slot supports controls of the following type: `text-input`, `number-input`, `checkbox` and `toggle`. You must define an `on-toggle` handler for `toggle` controls, or an `on-change` handler for the other supported controls. The name of the attribute is specified using `on-toggle-arg` for `toggle` controls, or `on-change-arg`.

The controls will be displayed below the attachment description field, or below the folder list if that option was enabled.

### Step 1: Define one or more controls with the `custom-options` slot.

```xml
<attachment-list id="attachmentList1" file-name-required="false" file-desc-required="false"
  datasource="attachmentds" show-folder-list="false" hide-when-empty="false" is-editable="true"
  show-managed-header="true" allow-naming="true"
  default-folder="CAD" record-marker-field-name="isdefault" record-marker-field-value="true"
  record-marker-icon="carbon:star--filled" check-deletable-item="checkDeletableItem"
>
  <checkbox slot="custom-options" label="Set as default" default-checked="true" checked="false"
    on-change="setAsDefault" on-change-arg="isdefault" id="ybm3n"
  />
  <toggle slot="custom-options" label="Analyse photo" toggle-label-off="No" toggle-label-on="Yes"
    type="TrueFalse" toggled="{page.state.analysePhoto}" on-toggle="setAnalysePhoto"
    on-toggle-arg="inferreq" id="bmyx8"
  />
  <number-input slot="custom-options" id="zaxve" label="Score" min="1" max="10" value="5" on-change="setScore"
    on-change-arg="score"
  />
  <text-input slot="custom-options" id="doctype1" label="Type" value="Images" on-change="setDocType"
    on-change-arg="doctype"
  />
</attachment-list>
```

### Step 2: Add event handlers for each custom control.

Two parameters are passed to each handler: the attribute name and the event emitted by the control. The event signature for `toggle` controls is `event.target.checked` (which will be true or false). The event signature for the other supported controls is `event.value`. Within the definition of the event handler you must call `event.onUpdate()` with two parameters: the attribute name and the attribute value. When the attachment is saved the payload will include the specified attribute and value.

Below are sample event handlers for the custom controls defined in the previous attachment list declaration.

```js
  /* checkbox */
  setAsDefault(attr, event) {
    log.i(TAG, 'setAsDefault: ', attr + '=' + event?.value);
    event.onUpdate(attr, event?.value);
  }

  /* toggle */
  setAnalysePhoto(attr, event) {
    log.i(TAG, 'setAnalysePhoto: ', attr + '=' + event?.target?.checked);
    this.page.state.analysePhoto = event?.target?.checked;
    event.onUpdate(attr, event?.target?.checked);
  }

  /* number input */
  setScore(attr, event) {
    log.i(TAG, 'setScore: ', attr + '=' + event?.value);
    event.onUpdate(attr, event?.value);
  }

  /* text input */
  setDocType(attr, event) {
    log.i(TAG, 'setDocType: ', attr + '=' + event?.value);
    event.onUpdate(attr, event?.value);
  }
```

![Adding an attachment with custom options](../assets/add-attachment-custom-options.png)

